    "background_story": "Kamila was a coal miner's daughter who grew up in a small town surrounded by the rugged beauty of the Appalachian Mountains. From a young age, she was fascinated by the stories of her father's work deep beneath the earth. When he passed away in a tragic accident, Kamila felt a sense of responsibility to carry on his legacy. She became a pitprop, installing wooden supports to hold up the mine's roof and ensure the safety of her fellow miners. Kamila's precision and attention to detail earned her the respect of the entire crew. She took pride in knowing that her work was crucial to the mine's operation, and that she was helping to bring coal to families in need. As a pitprop, Kamila found a sense of purpose and connection to her father's memory, working tirelessly to keep the mine safe and productive.",
